-ce27-4f0b-8124-bea5b733146e/effecf50-d6b2-11ed-8608-b9646d8e6014/file-1lg95txom.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lg95txol/f68eae54-ce27-4f0b-8124-bea5b733146e/effecf50-d6b2-11ed-8608-b9646d8e6014/file-1lg95txom.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lg95txol/f68eae54-ce27-4f0b-8124-bea5b733146e/effecf50-d6b2-11ed-8608-b9646d8e6014/file-1lg95txom.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lg95txol/f68eae54-ce27-4f0b-8124-bea5b733146e/effecf50-d6b2-11ed-8608-b9646d8e6014/file-1lg95txom.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lg95txol/f68eae54-ce27-4f0b-8124-bea5b733146e/effecf50-d6b2-11ed-8608-b9646d8e6014/file-1lg95txom.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lg95txol/f68eae54-ce27-4f0b-8124-bea5b733146e/effecf50-d6b2-11ed-8608-b9646d8e6014/file-1lg95txom.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The alkyl bromide reacts with Mg to form alkyl magnesium bromide (Grignard reagent) which attacks carbon dioxide followed by hydrolysis to form a carboxylic acid (compound J).</p>\n<p>It reacts with thionyl chloride (compound K) to form acid chloride.</p>"}]}